oTraiL Screen for Debian 12

This package shares one selected X11 window with the oTraiL Android app using
x11vnc and an ADB reverse TCP tunnel. The VNC server binds to localhost only;
the tunnel is available only through an authorized ADB device.

1. Connect the phone over USB, enable Android USB debugging, and authorize this laptop.
2. Run `otrail-screen windows` in the logged-in graphical desktop session.
3. Run `otrail-screen start N`, using a number from the current window list.
4. In oTraiL, open the heptagonal desktop-control icon and tap Connect.
5. Run `otrail-screen switch N` to share a different window or `otrail-screen stop`
   to terminate sharing and remove the ADB reverse tunnel.

This initial release supports X11 windows. In a Wayland session, wmctrl and x11vnc
can access only XWayland windows; native Wayland capture requires compositor
permission portals and is not provided by this package. The screen-sharing command
must run as the logged-in desktop user, not as root or through sudo.

The Android client uses raw RFB/VNC over the local ADB reverse tunnel. Do not remove
the localhost binding or expose the VNC port on a network interface.
